10.1177/0016986220932533,fc67e05e8823cd82,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Terman’s study was the first to systematically document the lives of the intellectually gifted. This cross-sectional study replicates and extends some of Terman’s findings on characteristics of the gifted in childhood, comparing largely unselected samples of gifted ( n = 50) and average-ability ( n = 50) adolescents matched by means of propensity score matching."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Results support Terman’s findings on gifted individuals’ psychological functioning and contradict negative stereotypes about the gifted."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract explicitly supports Terman’s findings. The particular original publication cannot be distinguished from the abstract.""}"
10.1007/s11409-020-09235-7,89fa4d08f8342512,0,10.1016/j.jecp.2011.02.005,Generating keywords improves metacomprehension and self-regulation in elementary and middle school children.,"De Bruin, A. B. H., Thiede, K. W., Camp, G., & Redford, J.",2011,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""De Bruin, A. B. H., Thiede, K. W., Camp, G., & Redford, J."", ""year"": ""2011"", ""title"": ""Generating keywords improves metacomprehension and self-regulation in elementary and middle school children."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.jecp.2011.02.005"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In line with our\nreplication hypothesis\n, we successfully replicated and thereby contributed to validating that generating delayed keywords is a promising activity to enhance the accuracy with which learners can discriminate between their differential comprehension for certain texts compared to others (see also e.g., De Bruin et al.\n2011\n; Thiede et al.\n2003\n,\n2005\n,\n2017\n)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In line with our\nreplication hypothesis\n, we successfully replicated and thereby contributed to validating that generating delayed keywords is a promising activity to enhance the accuracy with which learners can discriminate between their differential comprehension for certain texts compared to others (see also e.g., De Bruin et al.\n2011\n; Thiede et al.\n2003\n,\n2005\n,\n2017\n)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly report successful replication of the relative-accuracy keyword effect and identify these prior studies as the corroborated set. Bias and the expert-keyword optimization are extensions.""}"
