ble, Marinović & Pauen, 2010), with procedural changes based on both our novel experimental goals and the original authors’ advice."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""On the other hand, we failed to reproduce evidence that 18-month-old infants’ expectations are violated when an experimenter who ought to have a false belief reaches for an object in its true location (e.g. Onishi & Baillargeon, 2005; Song et al., 2008; Träuble et al., 2010)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Author verdict explicitly identifies this original; limitations do not replace that verdict.""}"
