dex"": 4, ""verdict"": ""blind_right""}","{""authors"": ""Sanders, M. A., Shirk, S. D., Burgin, C. J., & Martin, L. L."", ""year"": ""2012"", ""title"": ""The gargle effect rinsing the mouth with glucose enhances self-control."", ""doi"": ""10.1177/0956797612450034"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Importantly, this implies that, despite applying a powerful research design, the present study could not replicate the ﬁndings presented by Hagger and Chatzisarantis (2012), Molden et al. (2012) and Sanders et al. (2012)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Importantly, this implies that, despite applying a powerful research design, the present study could not replicate the ﬁndings presented by Hagger and Chatzisarantis (2012), Molden et al. (2012) and Sanders et al. (2012)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly report failure to replicate this published glucose effect. Limitations are discussed, but their substantive overall judgment remains failure, rather than an inability to adjudicate.""}"
