nt with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly compare their own result with this cited original finding. The stated agreement or disagreement determines this target’s outcome.""}"
10.23668/psycharchives.4766,3617489aca51758c,9,,"Primary teacher mathematics anxiety, teacher efficacy and mathematics avoidance.","Jaggernauth, S., & Jameson-Charles, M.",2015,full_text,,correct,argon,"{""target_index"": 9, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""shipped_right"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""The current study has two aims: The first aim is to conceptually replicate the finding of the meta-analysis by Hembree (1990) that math anxiety is higher for elementary school teachers than for students from other fields. The replication is relevant because the math anxiety of elementary school teachers has consequences for their pupils and it is necessary because previous studies have reported divergent levels of math anxiety, mostly lacked a reference sample, and almost exclusively were based on pre-service teachers. The second aim addresses whether all elementary school teachers experience math anxiety by the consideration of gender, specialization, and experience."", ""location"": ""introduction, p. 278"", ""reason"": ""Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles (2015) is cited only as background and literature context regarding math avoidance and teacher efficacy under the second aim, not as a replication target.""}","{""authors"": ""Jaggernauth, S., & Jameson-Charles, M."", ""year"": ""2015"", ""title"": ""Primary teacher mathematics anxiety, teacher efficacy and mathematics avoidance."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Nevertheless, our results were consistent with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Nevertheless, our results were consistent with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly compare their own result with this cited original finding. The stated agreement or disagreement determines this target’s outcome.""}"
10.23668/psycharchives.4766,3617489aca51758c,10,10.1111/j.1949-8594.2006.tb17921.x,Mathematics anxiety and mathematics teacher efficacy: What is the relationship in elementary preservice teachers?,"Swars, S. L., Daane, C. J., & Giesen, J.",2006,full_text,,correct,argon,"{""target_index"": 10, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""shipped_right"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""The current study has two aims: The first aim is to conceptually replicate the finding of the meta-analysis by Hembree (1990) that math anxiety is higher for elementary school teachers than for students from other fields. The replication is relevant because the math anxiety of elementary school teachers has consequences for their pupils and it is necessary because previous studies have reported divergent levels of math anxiety, mostly lacked a reference sample, and almost exclusively were based on pre-service teachers. The second aim addresses whether all elementary school teachers experience math anxiety by the consideration of gender, specialization, and experience."", ""location"": ""introduction, p. 278"", ""reason"": ""Swars et al. (2006) is cited only as background and discussion context regarding teacher efficacy under the second aim, not as a replication target.""}","{""authors"": ""Swars, S. L., Daane, C. J., & Giesen, J."", ""year"": ""2006"", ""title"": ""Mathematics anxiety and mathematics teacher efficacy: What is the relationship in elementary preservice teachers?"", ""doi"": ""10.1111/j.1949-8594.2006.tb17921.x"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Nevertheless, our results were consistent with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Nevertheless, our results were consistent with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly compare their own result with this cited original finding. The stated agreement or disagreement determines this target’s outcome.""}"
10.23668/psycharchives.4766,3617489aca51758c,11,10.1111/ssm.12320,From numbers to narratives: Preservice teachers experiences’ with mathematics anxiety and mathematics teaching anxiety.,"Olson, A. M., & Stoehr, K. J.",2019,full_text,,correct,argon,"{""target_index"": 11, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""shipped_right"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""Nevertheless, our results were consistent with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""location"": ""discussion, p. 287"", ""reason"": ""Olson & Stoehr (2019) is mentioned only once in the discussion as broader literature context on teaching anxiety and is not a replication target.""}","{""authors"": ""Olson, A. M., & Stoehr, K. J."", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": ""From numbers to narratives: Preservice teachers experiences’ with mathematics anxiety and mathematics teaching anxiety."", ""doi"": ""10.1111/ssm.12320"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Nevertheless, our results were consistent with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Nevertheless, our results were consistent with previous studies showing the relation of math anxiety to confidence (Brady & Bowd, 2005; Bursal & Paznokas, 2006), efficacy (Gresham, 2008; Jaggernauth & Jameson-Charles, 2015; Swars et al., 2006) and anxiety of teaching math (Ganley et al., 2019; Olson & Stoehr, 2019)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly compare their own result with this cited original finding. The stated agreement or disagreement determines this target’s outcome.""}"
10.23668/psycharchives.4766,3617489aca51758c,12,10.21449/ijate.615640,An English version of the mathematics teaching anxiety scale.,"Hunt, T. E., & Sari, M. H.",2019,full_text,,correct,argon,"{""target_index"": 12, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""shipped_right"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""However, in contrast to previous data (Hunt & Sari, 2019), our results provided no evidence of a beneficial effect of teaching math on the teachers’ attitudes, because female in-service and pre-service elementary school teachers did not significantly differ in enjoyment and ease of teaching math, and experience level in female in-service teachers did not significantly alter their teaching attitudes."", ""location"": ""discussion, p. 287"", ""reason"": ""Hunt & Sari (2019) appears only in the discussion as a post-hoc literature contrast for the secondary teaching-attitudes analysis and is not a replication target.""}","{""authors"": ""Hunt, T. E., & Sari, M. H."", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": ""An English version of the mathematics teaching anxiety scale."", ""doi"": ""10.21449/ijate.615640"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""However, in contrast to previous data (Hunt & Sari, 2019), our results provided no evidence of a beneficial effect of teaching math on the teachers’ attitudes, because female in-service and pre-service elementary school teachers did not significantly differ in enjoyment and ease of teaching math, and experience level in female in-service teachers did not significantly alter their teaching attitudes."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""However, in contrast to previous data (Hunt & Sari, 2019), our results provided no evidence of a beneficial effect of teaching math on the teachers’ attitudes, because female in-service and pre-service elementary school teachers did not significantly differ in enjoyment and ease of teaching math, and experience level in female in-service teachers did not significantly alter their teaching attitudes."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly compare their own result with this cited original finding. The stated agreement or disagreement determines this target’s outcome.""}"
10.31235/osf.io/zugae,ad7125f74e82a532,1,10.4324/9781315696485,The Effect of Firearms on Suicide.,"Kleck, G.",2018,full_text,,correct,argon,"{""target_index"": 1, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""shipped_right"", ""corrected_value"": null, ""quote"": ""Using a Poisson\nregression with the data in Kleck (2018, Table 17.3), I compared lethality of firearm (258,386 deaths, 308,623\nattempts, 83.7% lethal) and hanging/suffocation suicide attempts (118,072 deaths, 154,013 attempts, 76.7%\nlethal). Firearm suicide attempts are 8.8% more deadly, or conversely, hanging/suffocation attempts are 36.0%\nmore surivavable (both p < 0.001)."", ""location"": ""Introduction, p. 5, Footnote 2, lines 115-119"", ""reason"": ""Kleck (2018) is discussed only in the Introduction as background critique motivating the study, with an incidental footnote calculation on two summary counts from Table 17.3. The paper's Study Aims ('Given these concerns, I reproduce the study in Kleck (2021)'), Methods, Results, and Conclusion exclusively target Kleck (2021), so Kleck (2018) is not an omitted target.""}","{""authors"": ""Kleck, G."", ""year"": ""2018"", ""title"": ""The Effect of Firearms on Suicide."", ""doi"": ""10.4324/9781315696485"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Using a Poisson\nregression with the data in Kleck (2018, Table 17.3), I compared lethality of firearm (258,386 deaths, 308,623\nattempts, 83.7% lethal) and hanging/suffocation suicide attempts (118,072 deaths, 154,013 attempts, 76.7%\nlethal). Firearm suicide attempts are 8.8% more deadly, or conversely, hanging/suffocation attempts are 36.0%\nmore surivavable (both p < 0.001)."", ""outcome"": """", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""fulltext"", ""outcome_computation"": ""not checked"", ""outcome_computational_quote"": ""Using a Poisson\nregression with the data in Kleck (2018, Table 17.3), I compared lethality of firearm (258,386 deaths, 308,623\nattempts, 83.7% lethal) and hanging/suffocation suicide attempts (118,072 deaths, 154,013 attempts, 76.7%\nlethal). Firearm suicide attempts are 8.8% more deadly, or conversely, hanging/suffocation attempts are 36.0%\nmore surivavable (both p < 0.001)."", ""outcome_robustness"": ""robustness challenges"", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": ""Using a Poisson\nregression with the data in Kleck (2018, Table 17.3), I compared lethality of firearm (258,386 deaths, 308,623\nattempts, 83.7% lethal) and hanging/suffocation suicide attempts (118,072 deaths, 154,013 attempts, 76.7%\nlethal). Firearm suicide attempts are 8.8% more deadly, or conversely, hanging/suffocation attempts are 36.0%\nmore surivavable (both p < 0.001)."", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Footnote reanalyses the original published counts with Poisson regression, overturning the stated no-difference interpretation; it does not attempt to rerun original numbers.""}"
10.5964/jnc.6063,d667da1d0d43e70a,1,10.5951/AT.32.5.0051,A study of math anxiety/math avoidance in preservice elementary teachers.,"Kelly, W. P., & Tomhave, W. K.",1985,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Kelly, W. P., & Tomhave, W. K."", ""year"": ""1985"", ""title"": ""A study of math anxiety/math avoidance in preservice elementary teachers."", ""doi"": ""10.5951/AT.32.5.0051"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The current study replicated the finding that female elementary school teachers have a higher level of math anxiety in relation to female students from other fields (【10†Hembree, 1990】; 【26†Kelly & Tomhave, 1985】; 【32†Szczygieł & Cipora, 2016】)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The current study replicated the finding that female elementary school teachers have a higher level of math anxiety in relation to female students from other fields (【10†Hembree, 1990】; 【26†Kelly & Tomhave, 1985】; 【32†Szczygieł & Cipora, 2016】)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly state that this finding replicated. Specialization is an extension; smaller effects and inconclusive Bayes factors do not override their verdict.""}"
