10.1371/journal.pone.0246058,58d96ab64c094730,1,,Mitigation system threat partially mediates the effects of right-wing ideologies on climate change beliefs.,"Clarke EJ, Ling M, Kothe EJ, Klas A, Richardson B.",2019,full_text,,error,argon,"{""corrected_value"": {""authors"": ""Clarke EJ, Ling M, Kothe EJ, Klas A, Richardson B."", ""doi"": """", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""record_type"": ""replication"", ""title"": ""Mitigation system threat partially mediates the effects of right-wing ideologies on climate change beliefs."", ""year"": ""2019""}, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""file_key"": ""58d96ab64c094730"", ""location"": ""Introduction (lines 24-25); Study Two Results, Exploratory analyses on the dimensions of conservative ideology (line 122); Study Two Summary and conclusions (line 126); References 62 (line 243)"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""quote"": ""Participants invested in tradition, following those in power, and supporting the persecution of deviants (i.e., the dimensions of right-wing authoritarianism) also tended to report lower pro-environmentalism. When pitted against each other, we replicate recent findings that of these dimensions, SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate strongest unique associations with environmentalism [62]."", ""reason"": ""No prior adjudication or state file exists for this work. In addition to retesting Baldwin and Lammers' (2016, Ref 9, DOI 10.1073/pnas.1610834113, represented by shipped row 2384) temporal framing interaction across Studies One and Two, Study Two conducts a dedicated set of multiple regression analyses (reported in Results at line 122 and S11 Table, irrespective of experimental framing condition) pitting the two subdimensions of social dominance orientation (SDO-D, SDO-E) and three subdimensions of right-wing authoritarianism (Authoritarianism, Conservatism, Traditionalism) against each other as predictors of each environmentalism outcome. Both the Study Two Results (line 122) and Study Two Summary and conclusions (line 126) explicitly compare these unique associations to Clarke et al. (2019, Ref 62) and state that the analysis replicates Clarke et al.'s finding that SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate the strongest unique negative associations with environmentalism while the remaining subdimensions are weak and inconsistent predictors. Per review instructions, explicit empirical retesting in Results and Discussion is a valid replication target even when conducted in exploratory analyses and discussed in the Introduction. Because Clarke et al. (2019) is a distinct original paper and finding absent from shipped row 2384, target_index 1 is a genuinely missing original target."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0041_58d96ab64c094730"", ""target_index"": 1, ""verdict"": ""blind_right""}","{""authors"": ""Clarke EJ, Ling M, Kothe EJ, Klas A, Richardson B."", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": ""Mitigation system threat partially mediates the effects of right-wing ideologies on climate change beliefs."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""When pitted against each other, we replicate recent findings that of these dimensions, SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate strongest unique associations with environmentalism [62]."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""When pitted against each other, we replicate recent findings that of these dimensions, SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate strongest unique associations with environmentalism [62]."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly state replication of this original paper’s finding about the strongest unique ideological associations. This is an additional retested finding in the exploratory analyses.""}"
10.30707/etd2019.george.a,f5cd9ebc971eb837,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Our research replicates a previous study, which examined how Christians being led to believe God will either include or exclude them influenced well-being scores."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract confirms the exclusion hypothesis but also reports an absent moderation; it gives neither the original results nor an overall replication verdict. It therefore cannot settle agreement across the original findings.""}"
10.1891/jcop.2005.19.4.309,63030915d136ccf9,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,"{""corrected_value"": null, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""file_key"": ""63030915d136ccf9"", ""location"": ""Abstract, line 3"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""quote"": ""Research to date suggests that the best treatment for many mental disorders is provided through the combination of medications and psychotherapy (e.g., Hollon, Thase, & Markowitz, 2002). However, the majority of studies supporting this point have been done utilizing highly restricted, controlled samples that may not accurately reflect the way mental illness is treated in the community. The present study attempted to replicate those findings in an outpatient community clinic."", ""reason"": ""No prior adjudication or state file exists for this work. The supplied primary source contains only the abstract, which cites Hollon, Thase, and Markowitz (2002) (shipped row input_row_index 2389, DOI 10.1111/1529-1006.00008, a review article in Psychological Science in the Public Interest) with 'e.g.' as an example of the broader literature before stating that 'the majority of studies supporting this point have been done utilizing highly restricted, controlled samples' and that the present study 'attempted to replicate those findings in an outpatient community clinic.' Unresolved question: without the full text and reference list, the available evidence does not settle whether the paper empirically retests specific controlled-sample primary study findings absent from shipped row 2389, treats Hollon et al. (2002) as the sole target representing that claim, or tests only a general literature claim."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0047_63030915d136ccf9"", ""target_index"": 0, ""verdict"": ""undeterminable""}","{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Research to date suggests that the best treatment for many mental disorders is provided through the combination of medications and psychotherapy (e.g., Hollon, Thase, & Markowitz, 2002). However, the majority of studies supporting this point have been done utilizing highly restricted, controlled samples that may not accurately reflect the way mental illness is treated in the community. The present study attempted to replicate those findings in an outpatient community clinic."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Results showed that clients who took medications fared no better than clients who did not. These preliminary findings suggest that the combination of medications and psychotherapy may not be as effective in the “real world” as prior studies have implied, and point to the need for further research utilizing community samples."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The original claim of superior outcomes with combined medication and psychotherapy was explicitly retested. Authors report no advantage for combined treatment and contrast that result with prior findings.""}"
10.1037/xlm0000491,5f2326670f333040,1,,Positive recency in delayed free recall,"Tzeng, OJL",1973,full_text,,error,obvious,"{""field"": ""missing_row"", ""target_index"": 1, ""method"": ""obvious"", ""verdict"": ""blind_right"", ""corrected_value"": {""authors"": ""Tzeng, OJL"", ""year"": ""1973"", ""title"": ""Positive recency in delayed free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""record_type"": ""replication"", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined""}, ""quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g.\nTzeng, 1973\n;\nBjork & Whitten, 1974\n) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor.\n"", ""location"": ""Independent parent primary-source context; exhausted_candidate_0029.parent.json raw offsets"", ""reason"": ""Parent independently read own Experiment2 CDFR/DFR/IFR analyses and exact printed references. Authors explicitly reexamine negative recency after continual distractors because Tzeng1973andBjork/Whitten1974reported mixed/conflicting results. These are directly identified earlier empirical tests of the distractor variant assessed by this new experiment, not merely ancestors of the shipped Craik1970immediate-recall effect. Two independently published papers are cited for the conflicting relevant findings and both are explicitly re-tested; neither is a different version of Craik. This source-backed missing identity has unknown outcome because this decision only audits the pairing.""}","{""authors"": ""Tzeng, OJL"", ""year"": ""1973"", ""title"": ""Positive recency in delayed free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g. Tzeng, 1973 ; Bjork & Whitten, 1974 ) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors reexamine the prior CDFR findings jointly, but say only that previous studies had mixed results. They do not identify Tzeng’s original negative-recency result separately, so its agreement with the present robust negative recency cannot be determined.""}"
10.1037/xlm0000491,5f2326670f333040,2,,Recency-sensitive retrieval processes in long-term free recall,"Bjork, RA; Whitten, WB",1974,full_text,,error,obvious,"{""field"": ""missing_row"", ""target_index"": 2, ""method"": ""obvious"", ""verdict"": ""blind_right"", ""corrected_value"": {""authors"": ""Bjork, RA; Whitten, WB"", ""year"": ""1974"", ""title"": ""Recency-sensitive retrieval processes in long-term free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""record_type"": ""replication"", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined""}, ""quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g.\nTzeng, 1973\n;\nBjork & Whitten, 1974\n) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor.\n"", ""location"": ""Independent parent primary-source context; exhausted_candidate_0029.parent.json raw offsets"", ""reason"": ""Parent independently read own Experiment2 CDFR/DFR/IFR analyses and exact printed references. Authors explicitly reexamine negative recency after continual distractors because Tzeng1973andBjork/Whitten1974reported mixed/conflicting results. These are directly identified earlier empirical tests of the distractor variant assessed by this new experiment, not merely ancestors of the shipped Craik1970immediate-recall effect. Two independently published papers are cited for the conflicting relevant findings and both are explicitly re-tested; neither is a different version of Craik. This source-backed missing identity has unknown outcome because this decision only audits the pairing.""}","{""authors"": ""Bjork, RA; Whitten, WB"", ""year"": ""1974"", ""title"": ""Recency-sensitive retrieval processes in long-term free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g. Tzeng, 1973 ; Bjork & Whitten, 1974 ) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The prior CDFR studies are jointly described as yielding mixed results without assigning individual findings. Present negative recency is clear, but agreement with this specific original is not established in the supplied article.""}"
