10.31234/osf.io/akz6b,834b55f482c6e8a1,0,10.1016/j.brainres.2018.05.034,"Oxytocin receptor antagonist atosiban impairs consolidation, but not reconsolidation of contextual fear memory in rats.","Abdullahi, P. R., Eskandarian, S., Ghanbari, A., & Rashidy-Pour, A.",2018,full_text,,error,argon,"{""corrected_value"": {""authors"": ""Abdullahi, P. R., Eskandarian, S., Ghanbari, A., & Rashidy-Pour, A."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.brainres.2018.05.034"", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""record_type"": ""replication"", ""title"": ""Oxytocin receptor antagonist atosiban impairs consolidation, but not reconsolidation of contextual fear memory in rats."", ""year"": ""2018""}, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""file_key"": ""834b55f482c6e8a1"", ""location"": ""Discussion, Section 4, p. 15; Table 2, p. 3; References, p. 19"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""quote"": ""To this aim, we set out to conceptually \nor directly replicate previous studies in which systemic, post-reactivation administration of midazolam (MDZ, \nsee  Table  1),  propranolol  (PROP,  see  Table  2),  or  cycloheximide  (CYCLO;  Haubrich  et  al.,  2015)  resulted  in \namnesia for contextual fear memories."", ""reason"": ""No prior adjudication file exists (prior state recorded an unresolved CLI timeout). Contrary to the Luna triage objection claiming this paper is cited in the reference list only for atosiban, Abdullahi et al. (2018) is explicitly included in Table 2 (spelled 'Adbullahi et al. (2018)', Lab I, Fig. 5B, 90 s reactivation session, 5 mg/kg systemic propranolol, N = 12, Cohen's d = 1.19) for its positive-control experiment showing that post-reactivation systemic propranolol (PROP) disrupts contextual fear memory reconsolidation in rats. The authors explicitly state in the Discussion (and Abstract/Introduction/Results 3.1) that they set out to conceptually replicate the Table 2 systemic post-reactivation PROP studies across 12 PROP experiments and compare their null meta-analytic and experimental results against the Table 2 effect sizes. The only shipped row (input_row_index 2487, Alfei et al., 2015, doi: 10.1101/lm.038513.115) is a different original study from a different laboratory (Córdoba, Argentina vs. Semnan, Iran) testing midazolam rather than propranolol, and Abdullahi et al. (2018) is also distinct from the earlier Semnan propranolol studies (Abrari et al., 2008, Exp. 2, N = 20, d = 0.97; Taherian et al., 2014, Exp. 2, N = 24, d = 1.30)."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0063_834b55f482c6e8a1"", ""target_index"": 0, ""verdict"": ""blind_right""}","{""authors"": ""Abdullahi, P. R., Eskandarian, S., Ghanbari, A., & Rashidy-Pour, A."", ""year"": ""2018"", ""title"": ""Oxytocin receptor antagonist atosiban impairs consolidation, but not reconsolidation of contextual fear memory in rats."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.brainres.2018.05.034"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""To this aim, we set out to conceptually or directly replicate previous studies in which systemic, post-reactivation administration of midazolam (MDZ, see Table 1), propranolol (PROP, see Table 2), or cycloheximide (CYCLO; Haubrich et al., 2015) resulted in amnesia for contextual fear memories."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We can conclude that our findings are in stark contrast with the existing literature on post-reactivation amnesia in rats, in which systemic administration of MDZ (Table 1), PROP (Table 2), or CYCLO (Haubrich et al., 2015) has been shown to induce amnesia for contextual fear memories or other types of memories (Briggs & Olson, 2013; Dębiec & Ledoux, 2004; Flint & Marino, 2007; Milton, Lee, & Everitt, 2008; Przybyslawski et al., 1999; Robinson & Franklin, 2010; Taubenfeld et al., 2009)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly contrast their own results with this original or the target set containing it.""}"
