10.31234/osf.io/akz6b,834b55f482c6e8a1,10,10.1101/lm.045385.117,A comparison of behavioral and pharmacological interventions to attenuate reactivated fear memories.,"Ferrer Monti, R. I., Alfei, J. M., Mugnaini, M., Bueno, A. M., Beckers, T., Urcelay, G. P., & Molina, V. A.",2017,full_text,,error,argon,"{""corrected_value"": {""authors"": ""Ferrer Monti, R. I., Alfei, J. M., Mugnaini, M., Bueno, A. M., Beckers, T., Urcelay, G. P., & Molina, V. A."", ""doi"": ""10.1101/lm.045385.117"", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""record_type"": ""replication"", ""title"": ""A comparison of behavioral and pharmacological interventions to attenuate reactivated fear memories."", ""year"": ""2017""}, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""file_key"": ""834b55f482c6e8a1"", ""location"": ""Section 2.9.3-2.9.4 (Methods, lines 932-933, 955-956); Section 3.2-3.3 (Results, lines 1178-1179, 1200-1201, 1250-1251); References (lines 1781-1783)"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""quote"": ""First, experiments JA11 and JA12 constituted exact replications of the procedures reported in Alfei et al. (2015, \nexperiment 5) and Ferrer Monti et al. (2017, experiment 2)."", ""reason"": ""The prior adjudication file is absent and the prior state file records only an unresolved CLI timeout. The paper explicitly conducts direct/exact replications (experiments JA09, JA10, JA11, JA12, and NS09) and procedural variations (experiments NS10, NS12-NS14, NS18, NS21, including post-extinction MDZ in NS14) of Ferrer Monti et al. (2017, Experiment 2, 10.1101/lm.045385.117), testing whether systemic post-reactivation midazolam (3 mg/kg after a 2-min contextual fear reactivation session) induces amnesia. The only shipped row for this work is input_row_index 2487, which is Alfei et al. (2015, 10.1101/lm.038513.115). Although both original studies used the same 2-min reactivation and 3 mg/kg MDZ protocol in the Córdoba laboratory, Table 1 and Results Section 3.2 establish that they are independent published papers reporting distinct original experiments with different samples and effect sizes (Alfei et al., 2015, Exp. 5, N=18, d=1.80 vs. Ferrer Monti et al., 2017, Exp. 2, N=12, d=3.88), so report equivalence does not apply."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0064_834b55f482c6e8a1"", ""target_index"": 10, ""verdict"": ""blind_right""}","{""authors"": ""Ferrer Monti, R. I., Alfei, J. M., Mugnaini, M., Bueno, A. M., Beckers, T., Urcelay, G. P., & Molina, V. A."", ""year"": ""2017"", ""title"": ""A comparison of behavioral and pharmacological interventions to attenuate reactivated fear memories."", ""doi"": ""10.1101/lm.045385.117"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": ""Experiment 2"", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""JA09, JA10, JA11, JA12, NS09, NS10, NS12, NS13, NS14, NS18, NS21"", ""evidence_quote"": ""To this aim, we set out to conceptually or directly replicate previous studies in which systemic, post-reactivation administration of midazolam (MDZ, see Table 1), propranolol (PROP, see Table 2), or cycloheximide (CYCLO; Haubrich et al., 2015) resulted in amnesia for contextual fear memories."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Thus, in this series of exact replication attempts performed in two different labs at KU Leuven, we obtained no evidence for the induction of amnesia by post-reactivation MDZ administration, despite following the methodology of previous, successful studies as precisely as possible. In two exact replication attempts that were performed in the same lab as the original studies, we did find statistically significant effects of MDZ (Cohen’s d of .79 and .88), but the obtained effect sizes were smaller than those reported in prior publications (ranging between 1.80 and 3.88)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Original-lab exact replications supported the effect while other attempts failed.""}"
