ed row 2487 (Alfei et al., 2015), Piñeyro et al. (2013) is a separate primary paper reporting distinct experiments and is genuinely missing from the shipped dataset."", ""request_id"": ""luna_0065_834b55f482c6e8a1"", ""target_index"": 15, ""verdict"": ""blind_right""}","{""authors"": ""Piñeyro, M. E., Ferrer Monti, R. I., Alfei, J. M., Bueno, A. M., & Urcelay, G. P."", ""year"": ""2013"", ""title"": ""Memory destabilization is critical for the success of the reactivation-extinction procedure."", ""doi"": ""10.1101/lm.032714.113"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""To this aim, we set out to conceptually or directly replicate previous studies in which systemic, post-reactivation administration of midazolam (MDZ, see Table 1), propranolol (PROP, see Table 2), or cycloheximide (CYCLO; Haubrich et al., 2015) resulted in amnesia for contextual fear memories."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We can conclude that our findings are in stark contrast with the existing literature on post-reactivation amnesia in rats, in which systemic administration of MDZ (Table 1), PROP (Table 2), or CYCLO (Haubrich et al., 2015) has been shown to induce amnesia for contextual fear memories or other types of memories (Briggs & Olson, 2013; Dębiec & Ledoux, 2004; Flint & Marino, 2007; Milton, Lee, & Everitt, 2008; Przybyslawski et al., 1999; Robinson & Franklin, 2010; Taubenfeld et al., 2009)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly contrast their own results with this original or the target set containing it.""}"
